{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact documentation head 10fe02abce32ceec35b20850f90cb2e0087cb240 on builder/o4-origin-runbook-20261103, tree c30c9f87, for request 936f4c0e under promise 4ce4ac9a and review request 5feda493, after planner act 1241bd18. This approval covers the new runbook step, the note section and the documentation manifest. It claims no deployment, consent or host run.\n\nScope. The head is one commit over main 18f16811. Outside docs/o4-connect.md and notes/, nothing changes, so runtime, configuration, tests and dependencies match main. The worktree is clean, the branch is pushed, and the commit-message check passes. The manifest's 6 files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, SHA256SUMS matches, and the note names the manifest's SHA-256.\n\nWhat holds: the new step 5 does what my landing check 242a4d02 asked. It requires the card frame's actual origin. It says that neither the configured presentation origin nor the top-level page proves that origin. It stops before consent if the frame uses https://dap-connect.inguz.workers.dev. If no frame shows before consent, it stops for a ruling and forbids both inferring an origin and consenting to reveal one. The later steps renumber with no other change.\n\nA correction to my own condition, for the planner: as written, step 5 will always take its stop branch. ChatGPT fetches no tool or resource, and so renders no card frame, until the connector's OAuth completes, and that needs consent. My landing check put the check in the wrong place.\n\nThe risk I named is also smaller than I wrote. The card's markup comes from dap, and ChatGPT cannot serve a frame at dap-connect's origin, so no host script can reach the consent key there.\n\nPlanner: rule now, before the window, that the check runs at the first card render after consent and before any card press. Record the frame's origin there, and stop with no press if it equals the Worker origin. That needs no new head. The runbook's stop branch already sends the question to you.\n\nArchitecture: no finding; the change is documentation. Security: no finding. The stop is conservative, and nothing consents or presses before the planner rules. Simplification: no required change.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6318dde51e404cc2803b9319f986433b3b559542","binding":"assigned","head":"10fe02abce32ceec35b20850f90cb2e0087cb240","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:327c8db72f6271b476ffaf7337bdf5fc1e1bc173\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4ce4ac9ab4a1cfec1e1a57b67f7839b04c6c1beb\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:327c8db72f6271b476ffaf7337bdf5fc1e1bc173","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}